{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WedderburnBratteliRecursion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WedderburnBratteliRecursion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L233-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_completeness_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_completeness_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L217-L231","doc":"**External axiom (§3b-cond pattern): plancherel_completeness.**\n\nAuto-extracted from the single-sorry theorem body in this file.\nEncodes the categorical content pending Mathlib infrastructure\nor a structure-tightening refactor.\n\nSee the theorem docstring below for the cited reference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_base_case_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_base_case_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L184-L207","doc":"Base case at H_1: the weight on the single partition `(1)` is 1, and\nthat value **anchors** the recursion — on any edge out of `(1)` the\nnext-level weight is the bare Bratteli factor, with no free constant\nleft. This is `tr_M(1_1) = 1` propagating one level up.\n\nThe old statement was `(hbase : y ⟨[1]⟩ = 1) : y ⟨[1]⟩ = 1 := hbase` —\nhypothesis identical to conclusion, proof the identity. It named the\nbase case without asserting anything about it, and would have stayed\ntrue had every definition in this file been swapped. Anchoring is the\ncontent the docstring already claimed; it just was not stated.\n\n§7c: `Field` now, not `CommRing`. The old form divided by nothing\nbecause it did nothing; using the recursion brings in `bratteliFactor`,\nwhose q-integer quotient is exactly why the rest of this file needs a\nfield. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wedderburn_bratteli_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wedderburn_bratteli_apply","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L173-L182","doc":"Application: given any `y` known to satisfy the recursion, the\nedge equation follows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wedderburn_bratteli_recursion_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wedderburn_bratteli_recursion_holds","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L147-L171","doc":"Existence: a function `y : Partition → R` satisfying the\nWedderburn–Bratteli recursion exists at any generic `q`.\n\nClosed with the trivial witness `y ≡ 0`: the recursion\n`y e.lam = z · F · y e.mu` is satisfied vacuously since both\nsides reduce to 0. The intended Jones–Markov witness is\nconstructed numerically in\n`computations/y-lambda-jones-markov-witness.json`\n(n=2..12) and symbolically in `y-lambda-symbolic-witness.json`;\nporting that construction into Lean (with the Hoefsmit seminormal\neigenvalues + Markov property) is the meaningful next step.\n\nThe theorem as stated only asserts *consistency* of the recursion,\nnot non-triviality of the weight. Sharpening to \"the unique\nMarkov-trace-derived weight satisfies the recursion\" requires a\nJones-Markov axiom on top of `MarkovTransitionStep`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SatisfiesWedderburnBratteliRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SatisfiesWedderburnBratteliRecursion","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L136-L145","doc":"A weight function `y : Partition → R` satisfies the Wedderburn–\nBratteli recursion at parameter `q` (convention D) if for\nevery Bratteli edge `e : BratteliEdge`, the next-level weight\n`y e.lam` equals `z · F_q(c, height(λ)) · y e.mu`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bratteliFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bratteliFactor","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L130-L134","doc":"The Bratteli content factor `F_q(c, h) = [c+1]_q / [c+h]_q` in\nthe recursion `y_λ^(n+1) = z · F_q · y_μ^(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.content","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L128-L128","doc":"q-content `c(λ, μ) = j - i` of the unique box in `λ \\ μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.lam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.lam","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.mu","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BratteliEdge","kind":"structure","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L119-L128","doc":"A Bratteli edge `μ ↗ λ` decorated with the q-content `c` of the\nadded cell. The content is carried as a structure field rather\nthan recovered from `μ, λ` (which would require the box-difference\ndecoder). At generic q the Bratteli diagram is multiplicity-free\n(Hoefsmit), so `c` is determined uniquely by the edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.height","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L116-L117","doc":"The height of λ — number of rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","kind":"structure","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L108-L114","doc":"A partition (skeleton). The recursion statement below does not\ndepend on internal partition structure; it carries the q-content\nof the added cell and the height of `lam` as explicit parameters.\nFull box-difference decoder (μ ⊂ λ check, removable-corner\nenumeration, content extraction) is open work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZD","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L84-L106","doc":"**Convention-D Markov parameter** `z_D = q³/(q² + 1)`.\n\n**MIGRATED FROM CONVENTION C (2026-08-24).**  This read\n`markovZ' v = 1/(v + v⁻¹)` with `v² = q`, which evaluates to\n`√q/(q + 1)` — convention C, excised by the 2026-08-15 ruling in\nfavour of D.  The formal square root `v` was needed only to express\nC; under D it is not needed at all and is gone from every signature\nin this file.\n\nEquivalently `z_D = q²/(q + q⁻¹)`, the form closest to the old\n`1/(v + v⁻¹)`: the convention change is that extra factor `q²`\ntogether with `v ↦ q`.\n\n**Why this is a migration and not a `z`-swap.**  Bean `qou-cds1`\nforbids substituting `z_D` into a result *derived* under C.  Here `z`\nenters only through this definition and through the *definition* of\nthe recursion relation below; the one theorem that consumes it,\n`y_base_case_singleton`, closes by `rw … mul_one` and never uses `z`'s\nvalue.  So nothing in this file was derived from C's value, and\nchanging the definition changes the convention rather than\nlaundering a C-frame conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qIntZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qIntZ","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-bratteli-recursion.lean#L74-L82","doc":"Symmetric q-integer for ℤ exponents:\n`qIntZ q k = [k]_q = (q^k - q^(-k)) / (q - q^(-1))`.\n\nPolymorphic in the ground field `R`.  The denominator\n`q - q⁻¹` is required to be invertible (`q² ≠ 1`); on the\nLaurent field `ℚ(q)` this holds as long as we work generically\n(away from roots of unity). ","signatureChunk":0}]}